1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:08,325
A model, a harness, and a training programme to evaluate. This one is fictional, so the data can be shown freely.

2
00:00:10,070 --> 00:00:20,245
Three warehouse sites finished six weeks of training. A fourth, delayed site gives a fair comparison. The agent must decide what to pay the vendor.

3
00:00:21,970 --> 00:00:29,382
Seventeen files go in: ledgers, rules, minutes. A workbook and a decision memo must come out.

4
00:00:31,110 --> 00:00:37,897
The model works through Claude Code in a Docker container. The scoring rubric is sealed, out of its reach.

5
00:00:39,626 --> 00:00:48,263
It begins by looking at the data. A request goes out, Claude Code runs it in Docker, and the first rows of the test ledger come back.

6
00:00:49,990 --> 00:00:55,790
Then it writes a plan for itself: seven tasks, from reading the sources to writing the memo.

7
00:00:57,522 --> 00:01:06,147
It reads the rules too. A Word document comes back with the data boundary: individual results are for assessment and support only.

8
00:01:07,862 --> 00:01:12,187
Now it writes a long script that builds both deliverables from the sources.

9
00:01:13,930 --> 00:01:20,255
It runs the script. Seven source tables load, and the run ends with no error at all.

10
00:01:21,990 --> 00:01:30,052
But running without error is not the same as being right. The agent says it noticed issues, and checks who is actually in scope.

11
00:01:31,778 --> 00:01:38,790
So it opens its own script and edits it: the sample filter first, then the logic that decides the first work package.

12
00:01:40,510 --> 00:01:46,398
Then the same pipeline runs again. It succeeds again, now with the corrected scope.

13
00:01:48,114 --> 00:01:54,626
It checks the finished files. The workbook has nine sheets, the memo seventy-three paragraphs.

14
00:01:56,342 --> 00:02:04,104
The agent finishes. Only now does Harbor put the tests into the same container, and a separate judge session starts.

15
00:02:05,818 --> 00:02:13,793
The judge scores the two submitted files against thirty-four criteria, one at a time. Nothing flows back to the agent.

16
00:02:15,510 --> 00:02:23,997
Some things were right. The first work package was correctly judged conditional. But the second came out half a unit short.

17
00:02:25,730 --> 00:02:35,442
One penalty fired, and it is the most important one. Eight supervisors had too few chances to be rated, yet all were marked as not meeting the standard.

18
00:02:37,174 --> 00:02:47,249
The reward is point two zero eight. Six criteria met, twenty-two not met, one penalty. One pilot run, not a ranking.

19
00:02:48,978 --> 00:02:54,278
From professional task to agent run, independent check, and what to improve next.
